A||N||8||87GTBro||5 Cylinder Fiero!?  Someone help me find the other!||||1||
Z||000000||87GTBro||07-28-2001||07:12 PM||||I was at the drag strip last night and only ran my GT once.  The reason I only ran it once is because my friend informed me that the car was smoking really bad on hard acceleration.<P>It was pointed out to me that it was emitting black smoke which would suggest that it was running rich.  Later on TxFieros (aka Carlos) told me that my engine sounded like it was missing.<P>Sure enough, I got under the hood with the engine running and started removing the wires from the distributor one at a time until I removed one that did not affect the engine at all.<P>I found one.  It is cylinder # 4 (The middle one against the firewall)  Now that I knew which cylinder wasn't firing... I did the following:  Checked spark plug (had oily stuff on it), spark plugs are brand new (three days old), checked compression on cylinder (78 lbs, same as cyl. #5), spark plug wire (same problem), swapped spark plug with different cylinder (same problem).  Rotor is a year old.  Checked spark on wire by connecting another spark plug to wire and grounding the electrode out (good spark).<P>This is where I need help.  Is there anything I am leaving out on the ignition side?  If not, then my problem will be in the fuel system.<P>I think I know what it is, but I would like another opinion.  I think the injector in that cylinder is halfway clogged and is spraying a stream of gas into the cylinder instead of a fine spray.  The fuel is not igniting because it is not fine enough and that would explain the black smoke (rich condition).<P>Please tell me if I am overlooking something.  Thanks....<BR><P>------------------<BR>AOL IM: GTFiero86Dan<BR>'86 GT 4 speed<BR>'87 GT Auto<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/87GTBrosig1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Rogue_Ant||07-28-2001||07:22 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 87GTBro:<BR><B>I was at the drag strip last night and only ran my GT once.  The reason I only ran it once is because my friend informed me that the car was smoking really bad on hard acceleration.<P>It was pointed out to me that it was emitting black smoke which would suggest that it was running rich.  Later on TxFieros (aka Carlos) told me that my engine sounded like it was missing.<P>Sure enough, I got under the hood with the engine running and started removing the wires from the distributor one at a time until I removed one that did not affect the engine at all.<P>I found one.  It is cylinder # 4 (The middle one against the firewall)  Now that I knew which cylinder wasn't firing... I did the following:  Checked spark plug (had oily stuff on it), spark plugs are brand new (three days old), checked compression on cylinder (78 lbs, same as cyl. #5), spark plug wire (same problem), swapped spark plug with different cylinder (same problem).  Rotor is a year old.  Checked spark on wire by connecting another spark plug to wire and grounding the electrode out (good spark).<P>This is where I need help.  Is there anything I am leaving out on the ignition side?  If not, then my problem will be in the fuel system.<P>I think I know what it is, but I would like another opinion.  I think the injector in that cylinder is halfway clogged and is spraying a stream of gas into the cylinder instead of a fine spray.  The fuel is not igniting because it is not fine enough and that would explain the black smoke (rich condition).<P>Please tell me if I am overlooking something.  Thanks....<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Ok is it just me or is 78psi really low?  I think the service manual calls for 100psi min.  Also your fuel system doesn't have anything to do with your spark plug firing.  Pull the plug, put the wire on it, then ground the plug to something and see if it fires.  If it does then look at your fuel system (and also confirm your compression).  If your plug doesn't fire then it could be you have a crack in the cap, I would replace cap and rotor as just a good measurement anyway.<P>Rogue<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||07-28-2001||08:08 PM||||redo the compression test. Do all cylinders. make sure the throttle is blocked open and the injector fuses are both out.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Will||07-28-2001||11:02 PM||||Do the other tests first, but if you do find that the injector is stuck, rig up a hand held pushbutton to operate it, then tap the button several times with pressure behind the injector. The longer cycle time may help free up the injector if it isn't stuck too badly.<P>If it is stuck badly, pull it out and blow compressed air through it backwards.||||reg||1
Z||000004||87GTBro||07-29-2001||12:40 AM||||I already ruled out any possibility of the fault being in the ignition system.  The spark plug in that cylinder is getting plenty of spark.  The spark is just not lighting anything in the cylinder.  That's what lead me to think something is wrong with the injector.<P>I put some good fuel injector cleaner in my gas when I refueled and drove 80 miles this evening.  So far I have not felt or heard a difference in the way the engine is running.<P>When I got the pressure reading of 78 PSI, I may not have been doing it right.  I just took the spark plug out, screwed in the adapter, attached the gauge, unhooked the coil from the cap and cranked the engine over a couple of strokes.  I did not remove the fuel pump fuses or open the throttle.<P>I will try that tomorrow.  <P>------------------<BR>AOL IM: GTFiero86Dan<BR>'86 GT 4 speed<BR>'87 GT Auto<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/87GTBrosig1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||ray b||07-29-2001||01:20 AM||||well i hope itis just the spark or injector but if they don't fix it try a leak down test<BR>air pressure pumped in cyl and time the pressure drop slower the better. <BR>listening can give a clue whats bad rings or valves or cracks into oil or water passages.<BR>rich will give a dry soot[carbon] oily=oil leak.<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd||||reg||1
Z||000006||87GTBro||07-30-2001||08:00 PM||||*bump*||||reg||1
Z||000007||Darekin||07-30-2001||11:32 PM||||I have an 85 Fiero GT, and my compression is 2, 4, 6, is 150<BR>1, 5 is 140<BR>3 is 145<P>So you might want to get something checked.||||reg||1
Z||000008||87GTBro||08-02-2001||12:48 AM||||Just wanted to update everybody and let you know that I fixed the problem.  The cylinder was not receiving any gas.  The injectors were all screwed up.  I took the injectors out of my other GT and slapped em in there and the car runs great!<P>I realized that I have been running that poor car on 5 cylinders since I bought it 1.5 years ago without even knowing it!  <P>Now I really know what the 2.8 V6 is supposed to feel like and I must say that I am truly impressed!!!!  I probably gained 40 HP by changing out the injectors...<P>------------------<BR>AOL IM: GTFiero86Dan<BR>'86 GT 4 speed<BR>'87 GT Auto<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/87GTBrosig1.gif"> ||||reg||1
